IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa15-nouns`
IMPORT `coa15-ch4`
IMPORT `coa15-ch5`
IMPORT `coa-proc-purchase-of-own-shares`

-- coa-proc-purchase-of-own-shares-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-purchase-of-own-shares.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 690 to 723).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- Day 0 of each trace is the day named on the TIMELINE line of the rule, in calendar days.
-- Dates used: the meeting is on 1 March 2026, so the fifteen days of s 696(2)(b)(i) begin on 15 February 2026 (day 0) and the meeting is day 14.
-- The shares are delivered, and the resolution is passed, on 1 March 2026 (day 0 of those rules).
-- Ten years from 1 January 2027 end on 31 December 2036: 4,017 days after the contract of 1 January 2026 (eleven years less a day, three leap days in 2028, 2032 and 2036).
-- Ten years from 1 July 2026 end on 30 June 2036: 3,833 days after 1 January 2026.
-- Notices: the Gazette on 3 March (day 2), a newspaper on 5 March (day 4), a later Gazette on 8 March (day 7).

§ `Tests for the purchase of own shares procedure`

§§ `Fixtures`

-- the vote's fields, in order: the special-resolution answer; proposed at a meeting; a member holding shares to which it relates voted on it;
-- it would not have been passed without that vote; the directors' statement and auditor's report were made available to members.
`an effective vote` MEANS `ss 690-723 the vote` OF (JUST TRUE), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE
`a vote that a member's decisive vote makes ineffective` MEANS `ss 690-723 the vote` OF (JUST TRUE), TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
`a vote with no copy of the statement made available to members` MEANS `ss 690-723 the vote` OF (JUST TRUE), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`a vote on a resolution that is not a special resolution` MEANS `ss 690-723 the vote` OF (JUST FALSE), TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE

`a creditor` MEANS `s 721(1)(b) a creditor of the company`
`a member who did not vote in favour` MEANS `s 721(1)(a) a member of the company` OF FALSE
`a member who voted in favour` MEANS `s 721(1)(a) a member of the company` OF TRUE

§§ `Assertions on the helpers`

-- five weeks are 35 days and seven weeks are 49.
#ASSERT (`ss 690-723 the number of days in the weeks` 5) EQUALS 35
#ASSERT (`ss 690-723 the number of days in the weeks` 7) EQUALS 49
-- fifteen days ending with 1 March begin on 15 February (28 days in February 2026).
#ASSERT (`ss 690-723 the first of the fifteen days ending with the date of the meeting` (Date 1 3 2026)) EQUALS (Date 15 2 2026)
-- s 722(3): fifteen days, or the longer period the court directs; a period of 15 days or fewer directed does not shorten it.
#ASSERT (`ss 690-723 the days allowed for delivering a copy of the order` NOTHING) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT (`ss 690-723 the days allowed for delivering a copy of the order` (JUST 10)) EQUALS 15
#ASSERT (`ss 690-723 the days allowed for delivering a copy of the order` (JUST 30)) EQUALS 30
-- ss 716(1), 717(3), 718(3): a special resolution that no decisive vote of an interested member and no missing copy bars is effective.
#ASSERT `ss 690-723 the special resolution of section 716 is effective` (`an effective vote`)
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 690-723 the special resolution of section 716 is effective` (`a vote that a member's decisive vote makes ineffective`)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 690-723 the special resolution of section 716 is effective` (`a vote with no copy of the statement made available to members`)))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 690-723 the special resolution of section 716 is effective` (`a vote on a resolution that is not a special resolution`)))
-- ss 694(2), 695(3), 696(2)(b), 696(5): the contract is approved in advance on an authorising resolution, with fifteen days and the copy at the meeting, and no decisive interested vote.
#ASSERT `ss 690-723 the contract is approved in advance` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 690-723 the contract is approved in advance` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 690-723 the contract is approved in advance` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 16 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE))
#ASSERT (NOT (`ss 690-723 the contract is approved in advance` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE))
#ASSERT `ss 690-723 the contract is approved in advance` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE

§§ `Traces`

-- ---- s 696: the contract made available before the vote ----

-- s 696(2)(b): the copy is available at the registered office from day 0 (15 days ending with the meeting) and at the meeting itself on day 14, the meeting day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company makes the contract available before the vote (s 696)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 696(2)(b)(i) the company makes the copy or memorandum available for inspection at its registered office` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 696(2)(b)(ii) the company makes the copy or memorandum available for inspection at the meeting itself` AT 14

-- s 696(2)(b)(i): the copy is available at the registered office only from day 1, so for 14 days, not the 15 the text requires.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company makes the contract available before the vote (s 696)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 696(2)(b)(i) the company makes the copy or memorandum available for inspection at its registered office` AT 1

-- s 696(2)(b)(ii): the copy is available at the registered office in time but is not available at the meeting until day 15, after the meeting.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company makes the contract available before the vote (s 696)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 696(2)(b)(i) the company makes the copy or memorandum available for inspection at its registered office` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 696(2)(b)(ii) the company makes the copy or memorandum available for inspection at the meeting itself` AT 15

-- s 696(2)(a): a written resolution; the copy is sent to every eligible member on day 0, the day the proposed resolution is sent.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company makes the contract available before the vote (s 696)` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 696(2)(a) the company sends or submits the copy or memorandum to every eligible member` AT 0

-- s 696(1): the resolution is not one for the purposes of s 694, so the section does not apply and nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company makes the contract available before the vote (s 696)` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

-- ---- s 694: the bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved ----

-- ss 694(2)(a), 695(3), 696(2)(b), 696(5): the terms were authorised before the contract, the copy was available for 15 days and at the meeting, and no interested member's vote was decisive; the purchase on day 3 is allowed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company's bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved (s 694)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 694(1) the company makes the off-market purchase` AT 3

-- s 694(2): neither the terms were authorised before the contract nor does the contract bar purchases until they are; the purchase on day 3 is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company's bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved (s 694)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 694(1) the company makes the off-market purchase` AT 3

-- s 696(2)(b)(i), (5): the copy was available at the registered office only from 16 February, 14 days ending with the meeting, so the resolution is not validly passed and the purchase is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company's bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved (s 694)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 16 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 694(1) the company makes the off-market purchase` AT 3

-- s 695(3): a member holding shares to which the resolution relates voted and the resolution would not have been passed without the vote, so the resolution is not effective and the purchase is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company's bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved (s 694)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 694(1) the company makes the off-market purchase` AT 3

-- s 695(3)(b): a member holding shares to which the resolution relates voted, but the resolution would have been passed without the vote, so the bar does not bite and the purchase is allowed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company's bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved (s 694)` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 694(1) the company makes the off-market purchase` AT 3

-- s 696(2)(b)(ii), (5): the copy was not available at the meeting itself, so the resolution is not validly passed and the purchase is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company's bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved (s 694)` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 694(1) the company makes the off-market purchase` AT 3

-- s 694(2)(b): the contract provides that no shares may be purchased until its terms are authorised, and the vote and the copy are in order; the purchase is allowed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company's bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved (s 694)` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 694(1) the company makes the off-market purchase` AT 3

-- s 694(1): the contract is not approved and no purchase has been made by day 10; the bar stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company's bar on an off-market purchase until the contract is approved (s 694)` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 15 2 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- ---- s 702: the copy kept for ten years from the conclusion of the contract ----

-- s 702(3): the company stops keeping the copy available on day 100, long before the ten years from completion on 1 January 2027 have run.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the copy or memorandum available for ten years (s 702)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST (Date 1 1 2027)) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 702(3) the company stops keeping the copy or memorandum available for inspection` AT 100

-- s 702(3): the ten years beginning 1 January 2027 end on 31 December 2036, day 4017; stopping on that day leaves the copy unavailable on the last day.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the copy or memorandum available for ten years (s 702)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST (Date 1 1 2027)) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 702(3) the company stops keeping the copy or memorandum available for inspection` AT 4017

-- s 702(3): the company stops keeping the copy on day 4018, 1 January 2037, after the ten years have ended.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the copy or memorandum available for ten years (s 702)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) (JUST (Date 1 1 2027)) NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 702(3) the company stops keeping the copy or memorandum available for inspection` AT 4018

-- s 702(3): neither completion nor determination of the contract is known, so the ten years have not begun and stopping on day 100 is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the copy or memorandum available for ten years (s 702)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 702(3) the company stops keeping the copy or memorandum available for inspection` AT 100

-- s 702(3)(b): the contract otherwise determines on 1 July 2026 and is not completed; the ten years end on 30 June 2036, day 3833, and stopping on that day is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the copy or memorandum available for ten years (s 702)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 7 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 702(3) the company stops keeping the copy or memorandum available for inspection` AT 3833

-- s 702(3)(b): the same contract; stopping on day 3834, after the ten years, is no breach.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the copy or memorandum available for ten years (s 702)` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING (JUST (Date 1 7 2026)) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 702(3) the company stops keeping the copy or memorandum available for inspection` AT 3834

-- s 702(1): no contract approved under s 694 or authorised under s 701 has been entered into, so the section does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the copy or memorandum available for ten years (s 702)` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) NOTHING NOTHING AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- ---- s 702(5): the notice to the registrar of the place where the copy is kept ----

-- s 702(5), 703(1): the copy has not at all times been kept at the registered office; the notice on day 14 is in time (default is made for 14 days).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company gives notice of the place where the copy or memorandum is kept (s 702(5))` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 702(5) the company gives notice to the registrar of the place where the copy or memorandum is kept` AT 14

-- s 702(5), 703(1): the notice on day 15 is a default for 14 days.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company gives notice of the place where the copy or memorandum is kept (s 702(5))` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 702(5) the company gives notice to the registrar of the place where the copy or memorandum is kept` AT 15

-- s 702(5): the copy has at all times been kept at the registered office, so no notice is due.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company gives notice of the place where the copy or memorandum is kept (s 702(5))` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

-- ---- s 707: the return to the registrar ----

-- s 707(1): the return is delivered on day 27, the last day of the period of 28 days beginning with the delivery of the shares.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company delivers the return to the registrar (s 707)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 707(1) the company delivers the return to the registrar` AT 27

-- s 707(1): the return is delivered on day 28, after the period of 28 days.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company delivers the return to the registrar (s 707)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 707(1) the company delivers the return to the registrar` AT 28

-- s 707(1): no return by day 30.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company delivers the return to the registrar (s 707)` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 707(1): the company has not purchased shares under Chapter 4, so no return is due.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company delivers the return to the registrar (s 707)` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- ---- s 708: the notice of cancellation ----

-- s 708(1)(a): the shares were not bought out of distributable profits, so s 724 does not apply and they are cancelled; the notice on day 27 is in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company gives notice of cancellation to the registrar (s 708)` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 708(1) the company gives notice of cancellation to the registrar` AT 27

-- s 708(1): the notice on day 28 is after the period of 28 days beginning with the delivery.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company gives notice of cancellation to the registrar (s 708)` TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 708(1) the company gives notice of cancellation to the registrar` AT 28

-- s 708(1)(b): s 724 applies but the shares are cancelled forthwith; no notice by day 30 is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company gives notice of cancellation to the registrar (s 708)` TRUE TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 708(1): s 724 applies and the shares are held as treasury shares, not cancelled, so no notice of cancellation is due.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company gives notice of cancellation to the registrar (s 708)` TRUE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- ---- ss 714, 716, 719: the statement, the resolution and the notices ----

-- ss 716(2), 719(1), (2): the statement on day 0, the resolution on day 7 (the last day), the Gazette notice and the second notice on day 14, the last day, 7 days after the resolution.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`an effective vote`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the directors` DOES `s 714 the directors make the statement with the auditor's report annexed` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 716 the company passes the special resolution approving the payment out of capital` AT 7
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(1) the company causes the notice to be published in the Gazette` AT 14
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(2) the company publishes the notice in an appropriate national newspaper or gives it in writing to each creditor` AT 14

-- s 716(2): the resolution is passed on the day of the statement (day 0), which the text allows ("on, or within the week"); the notices follow on day 7 and day 3.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`an effective vote`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the directors` DOES `s 714 the directors make the statement with the auditor's report annexed` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 716 the company passes the special resolution approving the payment out of capital` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(2) the company publishes the notice in an appropriate national newspaper or gives it in writing to each creditor` AT 3
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(1) the company causes the notice to be published in the Gazette` AT 7

-- s 716(2): the resolution is passed on day 8, after the week.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`an effective vote`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the directors` DOES `s 714 the directors make the statement with the auditor's report annexed` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 716 the company passes the special resolution approving the payment out of capital` AT 8

-- s 719(1): the Gazette notice is published on day 15, 8 days after the resolution of day 7; the second notice was in time.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`an effective vote`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the directors` DOES `s 714 the directors make the statement with the auditor's report annexed` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 716 the company passes the special resolution approving the payment out of capital` AT 7
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(2) the company publishes the notice in an appropriate national newspaper or gives it in writing to each creditor` AT 14
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(1) the company causes the notice to be published in the Gazette` AT 15

-- s 719(2): the Gazette notice is published but neither a newspaper notice nor a notice in writing to each creditor is given by day 30.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`an effective vote`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the directors` DOES `s 714 the directors make the statement with the auditor's report annexed` AT 0
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 716 the company passes the special resolution approving the payment out of capital` AT 7
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(1) the company causes the notice to be published in the Gazette` AT 10
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 716(2): the statement is made on day 0 and the week for the resolution is still running at day 5.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`an effective vote`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the directors` DOES `s 714 the directors make the statement with the auditor's report annexed` AT 0
    (WAITUNTIL 5)

-- s 714(1): the directors have not made the statement and the text gives no time for it.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`an effective vote`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 709(1): the company is not a private limited company, so this chain does not arise.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` FALSE FALSE (`an effective vote`) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 717(3): a member holding shares to which the resolution relates voted, and it would not have been passed without the vote; the resolution is not effective, so the payment is not lawful (s 713(1)) and a payment on day 3 is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`a vote that a member's decisive vote makes ineffective`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 723(1) the company makes the payment out of capital` AT 3

-- s 718(3): the directors' statement and auditor's report were not made available to members, so the resolution is ineffective and a payment on day 3 is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 payment out of capital: the statement, the resolution and the notices (ss 714, 716, 719)` TRUE FALSE (`a vote with no copy of the statement made available to members`) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 723(1) the company makes the payment out of capital` AT 3

-- ---- s 719(4): the copy of the statement and report to the registrar ----

-- s 719(4): the first notice is the newspaper notice of 5 March (day 4), earlier than the Gazette notice of 8 March; the copy is delivered on day 4, the day of the first notice.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company delivers a copy of the statement and report to the registrar (s 719(4))` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 8 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(4) the company delivers to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report` AT 4

-- s 719(4): the copy is delivered on day 5, after the first notice of day 4.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company delivers a copy of the statement and report to the registrar (s 719(4))` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 8 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(4) the company delivers to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report` AT 5

-- s 719(4): no copy is delivered by day 10.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company delivers a copy of the statement and report to the registrar (s 719(4))` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 8 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 719(4): the Gazette notice of 3 March (day 2) is the first notice; the copy on day 2 is in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company delivers a copy of the statement and report to the registrar (s 719(4))` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 719(4) the company delivers to the registrar a copy of the directors' statement and auditor's report` AT 2

-- ---- s 720: the statement and report open to inspection ----

-- s 720(1): the statement and report are available from day 2, the day of the first notice (3 March), and stay available to day 35 and beyond.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the statement and report available for inspection (s 720)` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 720(1) the company makes the statement and report available for inspection` AT 2
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 720(1)(a): the statement and report are made available on day 3, after the day of the first notice.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the statement and report available for inspection (s 720)` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 720(1) the company makes the statement and report available for inspection` AT 3

-- s 720(1)(b): available from day 2 but withdrawn on day 20, before five weeks after the resolution.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the statement and report available for inspection (s 720)` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 720(1) the company makes the statement and report available for inspection` AT 2
    PARTY `ss 690-723 the company` DOES `s 720(1) the company stops keeping the statement and report available for inspection, or refuses an inspection` AT 20

-- s 720(1)(b): available from day 2 but withdrawn on day 35, so they are not available on the last day of the period.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `ss 690-723 the company keeps the statement and report available for inspection (s 720)` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 3 3 2026) (Date 5 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
