-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN:
-- Ten traces differ in class (FULFILLED, BREACH, RESIDUAL) between the unstable build (a50cbd0, 25 November 2026) and main (112). All 83 traces match their EXPECT on unstable; 73 match on main. Only the class was compared, not the printed form.
--   * line 382, `ss 690-723 the objection to the payment and the court's order (ss 721, 722)`, the creditor applies on day 36, after the five weeks: FULFILLED on unstable, RESIDUAL on main (main prints the applicants' duty to tell the registrar, s 722(1), as still open).
--   * line 387, the same rule, nobody applies by day 40: FULFILLED on unstable, RESIDUAL on main (main prints the s 722(1) duty as still open once the five weeks have lapsed: a lapsed MAY).
--   * lines 453, 458, 468, 478 and 483, `ss 690-723 the company makes the payment out of capital in the window (s 723)`, a payment on day 35, 49, 50, 56 and 57 (every one after the 34-day bar has lapsed): FULFILLED, FULFILLED, BREACH, FULFILLED and BREACH on unstable; RESIDUAL on main (main prints the window's MAY as still open and does not match the payment: an event after a bar's lapse).
--   * lines 520, 525 and 535, `ss 690-723 the shares are surrendered in the window (s 723(1A))`, a surrender on day 35, 49 and 50: FULFILLED, FULFILLED and BREACH on unstable; RESIDUAL on main (the same).
-- Every trace of day 34 or earlier in the two windows, the cancelled-resolution trace, and every other trace match in class on both.
-- No trace has both limbs of a RAND in breach, so the known difference on a RAND of two breaches is not exercised here.
